Damn, that happened so unexpectedly.

I started playing Nethack in 1999 after searching the 'net for the best
free game and found the site. Started lurking here in 2001 after many,
many deaths and kept playing, usually about 10 games a week for about
two weeks at a time and a month in between sessions. Yes - died pretty
often. I stopped playing last year about August due to the pressure
associated with getting my bachelors and didn't start again until end
of March, when I visited my parents and found that Nethack was still on
my home PC. Being bored, I played a bit and got further than ever
before - dying in Orcus Town due to carelessness (and playing after a
bit of a bender...) So with my Honors work piling up on me, I decided
to start playing again... on Thursday, 2 June. And look at what
happened... I said my first post here would be my first ascension
post... and I kept my promise.

Now, to the game.

It started off like any other. But on level 4 I found a altar and a BoH
and thought myself lucky. Went on to Sokoban... and guess what? Another
BoH. Got out of Sokoban and was XP5 so I dipped my longsword and 1st
time got Excalibur. Thought that was fun and proceeded to the mines.
2nd level of the mines gave me yet another BoH and by this time I was
getting worried. Minetown was an old bones pile of mine - the one in
the Top 10 list. Another BoH AND Mjollnir. And of course Ex-Excalibur
blessed rustproof +1 long sword. Oh, and a magic whistle which made pet
management a bit easier.

So off I went to Mine's End. Enroute my cat kicked the bucket and I
went petless from then on. Fat lot of use that whistle was... Got in
and out of the mines then and used all the fountains to created as much
water potions as I can. First altar I found I converted it all to Holy
Water and Blessed my BoH's. Needless to say, I named them to organize
my packrat attitude towards life.

On Dlvl8 I found helmet which turned out to be the HoB which I used up
to the last 2 turns of the game. Dlvl11 had the portal to Ludios which
I skipped for a while. And so I descended... all too aware that I had
neither reflection nor magic resistance. Dlvl13 was the Quest portal. I
eventually reached Dlvl17, which had a co-aligned temple. Clearing out
all non-essential potions, I prayed for Holy Water... and got not only
that, but got crowned as well! First time ever. And I didn't even get a
gift (I already had Excalibur.) Anyway, so I quickly blessed my stack
of 8 identify scrolls and identified all the stuff in my BoH's. I got
up to a respectable AC of -17. But still no MR of Reflection.

I plowed down to Medusa. Using my ring of levitation (same one used the
ENTIRE game) I moved over, quaffed a potion of blindness and used a
mirror on her. Perseus had what I needed. A shield of reflection. Now I
was ready for the quest.

Not much ado there, but on the last quest level I found a cloak of
magic resistance. Now I was kitted out! Surtur escaped upstairs and I
finished him off. Then on to Ludios I went. Killed all the soldier and
spent a while moving all the gloves and boots to the temple to find
better ones. Improved my AC to -20 (I replaced my cloak of protection
with the cloak of MR.) I used my magic markers found in the bones pile
to write a few enchant armors to get Red Dragon Scale Mail and fooproof
my [ofMR.

And yet again I was on the downward path. Got to the castle, cleaned it
out, and got the WoWishing. First source of wishes for the entire game.
And only one. Using a wand of enlightenment, I saw that I pretty much
only needed disintegration resistance, so a Black DSM was the option,
as well as Gauntlets of Power and Speed boots. Used a magic marker to
write a blessed scroll of charging and recharged the wand. Now I needed
blank scrolls so I also wished for a wand of cancellation.

Then I was writing scrolls of enchant armor. Accidentally vaporised my
[ofMR and wished up a new one as well. Wrote the marker dry and had an
AC of -25. Then I went up to the temple and got protection as much as
Ludios could buy and I was up to an AC of -35. Good show! Now I was
ready for Gehennom.

VoTD had speed boots (dammit!) but otherwise uneventful. Practised with
Mjollnir and Grayswandir to improve their skill levels should I need
them. Werebane was found in the Castle Armory, and Giantslayer lying
around in Gehennom. Left them in my BoH. I also found a wand of
polymorph and 5 scrolls of light were transformed into enchant weapon.
Tadaa! So I enchanted my main weapons.

I found a T-shirt in Asmodeus Lair and promptly put it on. A few
polypiles on, and I had another 3 enchant armors to use. AC was now -38
and looking good. Moved on downward, killed Vlad, found the two fake
towers, one which had a "ofReflection. Beaut! Switched it with my "oLS
(of which I now had two) and tried the #twoweapons thingie. Whooha!
Nothing could stand in my way! Moved to go get the Book from the
Wizard. Ate a few wraiths along the way to level up so that
twoweaponing could increase in skill. Used conflict to mow through the
baddies and killed Rodney with one of my 3 wands of death I had picked
up from the Gehennom denizens. And then things started getting hairy...

Point 1. Being a packrat, I was moving continually at burdened from
about turn 10000. Point 2. Malignant aura unblesses my BOH's and pulls
me down to stressed. Hell, that was irritating. Anyway, so I performed
the invocation, got down to the sanctum, conflict-mowed through the
crowed... and then Rodney Trouble Troubled me. Blew out a wand of death
as it kept missing him and had to use ol' Excalibur to do the job. But
got the Amulet at the end. Man, that was a rush. First time I ever saw
it.

Then came the Groot Trek to the top. ARRRR!! Bloody Mysterious force!
It kicked me down 2 levels at least 15 times. And it was so nice when
Rodney popped up on those no-teleport levels... but, I got through it.
Not without losses though. "Help me, my pets!" And sure as hell, 3
times it popped a mindflayer right next to me. I have a stack of
daggers for when they're squares away, but so close? I only had 2
scrolls of genocide the entire game - one went for Liches (the Castle
level was fun with them constantly summoning stuff!) and the other I
used to reverse-geno Tengu's to get TC after I got teleportitis from
the first tengu I ate. So there went half of my knowledge of my
inventory and it appears most of the levels I knew. I dug out gehennom,
so that wasn't too bad, but the normal dungeon... oooh, if I hadn't
only explored it about two days ago it would have taken much longer.

On the way up, I stopped by Ludios once again, to stack up on food.
While there, I noticed a plumed helmet lying around. After finding an
identify scroll in my BOH (after I'd gotten light and food detection
again) it turned out to be a HoOA. Great, just pop that in here, for
just in case...

HiHo HiHo its off to the planes we go... Earth saw Rodney get a Wand of
Death in the face, and my Ord of Fate located the portal for me. Dig,
dig dig with wands (no pick-axes the entire game, only mattocks - and
that screws up both shields and twoweaponing) and we hit air. Air
elementals pummeled me quite a bit, hitting me into the low 200's (max
HP 297) but I used the other vortexes to heal up. Ord of Fate, show me
the way, and it was up to Fire. Same story there. Then water... Orb of
Fate... There it is... and then its gone?!? Dammit, flying around on
water is irritating and it took me a while to find the portal.

Astral. Apparently conflict isn't such a good idea on astral? Tyr
certainly didn't like it. Anyway, I first went to the left, saw a
priestess of Odin, figured, neutral and went to the centre. There I saw
a priest of Loki and moved right. Right was Death and I hate that
bloody... anyway, running past him saw my max HP drop by about 80!
Quick, to the altar! Wha? Chaotic? No way I'm gonna survive Death
again. HoOA... and the choir sings...

Anyway, thats my story, mostly from memory. I'd like to hear some
comments. Oh, and what to do with death. For my next ascension (any
decade now) I'm gonna try archeologists or wizards... will see how it
goes.

Sincerely,
DollarD


